==Mechanics==
Normal ranged attacks of drakes can be fully blocked by [[Protect from Missiles]]. Unlike most enemies, Drakes can perform melee attacks when players stand diagonally from them. 

Drakes do '''not''' require [[dragonfire protection]] to be slain, unlike most other dragons. However, after seven auto-attacks, drakes will launch a volcanic breath towards the player's current position, which deals 6-8 damage for four hits if the player is struck by the projectile. The levels of dragonfire protection apply to this special attack: 

* Having a form of [[dragonfire]] protection will reduce this to 0-4 damage.
* Wielding a [[dragonfire shield]], [[dragonfire ward]], or [[anti-dragon shield]] alongside drinking an [[antifire potion]] will negate the damage.
* Using a [[super antifire potion]] or its [[Extended super antifire|extended]] version will negate the damage, allowing you to wear a defender or use a blowpipe.

Alternatively, moving one tile elsewhere when the projectile is launched allows complete avoidance. 

Using Protect from Missiles together with dragonfire protection will enable a player to take no damage when attacking at a distance.

